cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these write-ups, please cite them as below."
title: "Rentcraft: an open research log on teaching small neural networks to play a Monopoly-style board game"
authors:
  - alias: q3ok
version: "journal entry 1"
url: "https://github.com/q3ok/rentcraft"
repository-code: "https://github.com/q3ok/rentcraft"
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  Public write-ups of Rentcraft, a Monopoly-style board game written from scratch as a research testbed for
  game-playing AI: what we tried while teaching small neural networks (MLPs and transformers) to play it against
  strong rule-based bots, including open-ended trade negotiation, what worked, what did not, and the numbers
  behind it.
keywords:
  - reinforcement learning
  - imitation learning
  - board games
  - Monopoly-style game
  - negotiation
  - trading
  - PPO
  - DAgger
  - transformers
